.Dd February 19, 2026
.Dt ELF_BACKEND 3
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm elf_register_reloc_backend ,
.Nm struct elf_reloc_backend ,
.Nm elfobj_reloc_ctx_t
.Nd ELF relocation backend plugin interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In elfobj.h
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fo elf_register_reloc_backend
.Fa "const struct elf_reloc_backend *backend"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm libelfobj
library uses a plugin-based architecture for architecture-specific
relocation processing.
This allows the library to support multiple target architectures
without embedding architecture-specific code in the core library.
.Pp
Each backend provides functions to:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Apply relocations (compute final values).
.It
Query relocation sizes.
.It
Determine if relocations are PC-relative.
.El
.Ss Backend Structure
The
.Vt struct elf_reloc_backend
structure defines a relocation backend:
.Bd -literal
struct elf_reloc_backend {
    uint32_t machine;           /* Architecture identifier (EM_*) */
    int (*apply_reloc)(const elfobj_reloc_ctx_t *ctx,
                       uint32_t type,
                       uint64_t place,
                       uint64_t sym_value,
                       int64_t addend,
                       uint64_t *out_value);
    int (*reloc_size)(uint32_t type);
    int (*is_pc_relative)(uint32_t type);
};
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "apply_reloc"
.It Va machine
The ELF machine type for this backend.
Standard values include:
.Bl -tag -width "EM_X86_64" -compact
.It Dv EM_386
Intel 80386 (i386).
.It Dv EM_X86_64
AMD x86-64.
.It Dv EM_ARM
ARM.
.It Dv EM_AARCH64
ARM 64-bit.
.It Dv EM_MIPS
MIPS.
.It Dv EM_PPC
PowerPC.
.It Dv EM_PPC64
PowerPC 64-bit.
.It Dv EM_SPARC
SPARC.
.It Dv EM_SPARCV9
SPARC V9 64-bit.
.El
.It Va apply_reloc
Callback to compute the final relocation value.
Returns 0 on success, negative on error.
.It Va reloc_size
Callback to return the size in bytes of the relocation target.
Returns the size, or -1 for unknown relocation types.
.It Va is_pc_relative
Callback to determine if a relocation is PC-relative.
Returns non-zero if PC-relative, 0 otherwise.
.El
.Ss Relocation Context
The
.Vt elfobj_reloc_ctx_t
structure provides context for relocation processing:
.Bd -literal
typedef struct {
    uint32_t machine;           /* Target architecture */
    uint8_t use_rela;           /* Non-zero if using RELA format */
    uint8_t reserved[3];        /* Reserved for future use */
} elfobj_reloc_ctx_t;
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "use_rela"
.It Va machine
The target architecture for relocation.
.It Va use_rela
Non-zero if the relocation uses the RELA format (with explicit addend).
Zero if using REL format (implicit addend).
.El
.Ss Backend Registration
Backends are registered globally using
.Fn elf_register_reloc_backend .
The registration process:
.Bl -enum
.It
Validates the backend structure (non-NULL pointer, required callbacks).
.It
Checks if a backend for the same architecture already exists.
.It
Replaces the existing backend if found, or adds the new backend.
.El
.Pp
Backends persist for the lifetime of the process.
There is no function to unregister a backend.
.Ss Backend Callbacks
.Bl -tag -width "is_pc_relative"
.It Sy apply_reloc
The
.Fn apply_reloc
callback computes the final value to store at the relocation site:
.Bd -literal
int apply_reloc(const elfobj_reloc_ctx_t *ctx,
                uint32_t type,
                uint64_t place,
                uint64_t sym_value,
                int64_t addend,
                uint64_t *out_value);
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "out_value" -compact
.It Fa ctx
Relocation context (architecture, format).
.It Fa type
Architecture-specific relocation type.
.It Fa place
The address of the relocation site (P in ELF formulas).
.It Fa sym_value
The symbol value (S in ELF formulas).
.It Fa addend
The relocation addend (A in ELF formulas).
.It Fa out_value
Output parameter for the computed value.
.El
.Pp
The callback should:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Compute the final value according to the relocation type.
.It
Check for overflow and return an error if the value cannot be represented.
.It
Store the result in
.Fa *out_value .
.El
.Pp
Return 0 on success, negative on error.
.It Sy reloc_size
The
.Fn reloc_size
callback returns the size of the relocation target:
.Bd -literal
int reloc_size(uint32_t type);
.Ed
.Pp
Common sizes:
.Bl -bullet
.It
1 byte (8-bit relocations).
.It
2 bytes (16-bit relocations).
.It
4 bytes (32-bit relocations).
.It
8 bytes (64-bit relocations).
.El
.Pp
Return -1 for unknown relocation types.
.It Sy is_pc_relative
The
.Fn is_pc_relative
callback determines if a relocation is PC-relative:
.Bd -literal
int is_pc_relative(uint32_t type);
.Ed
.Pp
PC-relative relocations compute values relative to the relocation site.
This information is used for:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Relaxation optimization.
.It
Position-independent code handling.
.It
Linker diagnostics.
.El
.Pp
Return non-zero if PC-relative, 0 otherwise.
.El
.Ss Standard Backends
The library may include built-in backends for common architectures:
.Bl -tag -width "x86-64"
.It Sy i386
Supports
.Dv R_386_NONE ,
.Dv R_386_32 ,
.Dv R_386_PC32 ,
and other i386 relocation types.
.It Sy x86-64
Supports
.Dv R_X86_64_64 ,
.Dv R_X86_64_PC32 ,
.Dv R_X86_64_PLT32 ,
.Dv R_X86_64_GOTPCREL ,
and other x86-64 relocation types.
.El
.Pp
Applications can override built-in backends by registering a new
backend for the same architecture.
.Ss Thread Safety
Backend registration is thread-safe for concurrent registration of
different architectures.
However, concurrent registration of the same architecture from multiple
threads results in undefined behavior.
.Pp
Backend callbacks may be called concurrently from multiple threads
when processing different objects.
Callbacks must be thread-safe.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn elf_register_reloc_backend
returns
.Dv ELF_OK
on success.
.Pp
On failure, returns:
.Bl -tag -width "ELF_ERR_OOM"
.It Dv ELF_ERR_STATE
.Fa backend
is NULL or
.Fa backend->apply_reloc
is NULL.
.It Dv ELF_ERR_OOM
The maximum number of backends (16) has been reached.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss Implementing a Minimal Backend
.Bd -literal
#include <elfobj.h>
#include <stdio.h>

/* Minimal backend for a hypothetical 32-bit RISC architecture */
#define EM_MYRISC 0x9999

#define R_MYRISC_NONE   0
#define R_MYRISC_32     1  /* Absolute 32-bit */
#define R_MYRISC_PC32   2  /* PC-relative 32-bit */
#define R_MYRISC_HI16   3  /* High 16 bits */
#define R_MYRISC_LO16   4  /* Low 16 bits */

static int myrisc_apply_reloc(const elfobj_reloc_ctx_t *ctx,
                              uint32_t type,
                              uint64_t place,
                              uint64_t sym_value,
                              int64_t addend,
                              uint64_t *out_value) {
    int64_t result;

    switch (type) {
    case R_MYRISC_NONE:
        *out_value = 0;
        return 0;

    case R_MYRISC_32:
        result = (int64_t)sym_value + addend;
        if (result < 0 || result > 0xFFFFFFFFLL) {
            return -1;  /* Overflow */
        }
        *out_value = (uint64_t)result;
        return 0;

    case R_MYRISC_PC32:
        result = (int64_t)sym_value + addend - (int64_t)place;
        if (result < -0x80000000LL || result > 0x7FFFFFFFLL) {
            return -1;  /* Overflow */
        }
        *out_value = (uint64_t)result;
        return 0;

    case R_MYRISC_HI16:
        result = (int64_t)sym_value + addend;
        *out_value = ((uint64_t)result >> 16) & 0xFFFF;
        return 0;

    case R_MYRISC_LO16:
        result = (int64_t)sym_value + addend;
        *out_value = (uint64_t)result & 0xFFFF;
        return 0;

    default:
        return -1;  /* Unknown relocation */
    }
}

static int myrisc_reloc_size(uint32_t type) {
    switch (type) {
    case R_MYRISC_32:
    case R_MYRISC_PC32:
        return 4;
    case R_MYRISC_HI16:
    case R_MYRISC_LO16:
        return 2;
    default:
        return -1;
    }
}

static int myrisc_is_pc_relative(uint32_t type) {
    return type == R_MYRISC_PC32;
}

int main(void) {
    struct elf_reloc_backend backend = {
        .machine = EM_MYRISC,
        .apply_reloc = myrisc_apply_reloc,
        .reloc_size = myrisc_reloc_size,
        .is_pc_relative = myrisc_is_pc_relative,
    };

    elf_err_t err = elf_register_reloc_backend(&backend);
    if (err != ELF_OK) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Failed to register backend: %s\\n",
                elf_errstr(err));
        return 1;
    }

    printf("MYRISC backend registered successfully\\n");
    return 0;
}
.Ed
.Ss Implementing an x86-64 Backend
.Bd -literal
#include <elfobj.h>

/* Extended x86-64 backend with additional relocation types */
#define R_X86_64_64         1
#define R_X86_64_PC32       2
#define R_X86_64_GOT32      3
#define R_X86_64_PLT32      4
#define R_X86_64_GOTPCREL   9
#define R_X86_64_32        10
#define R_X86_64_32S       11

static int x86_64_apply_reloc(const elfobj_reloc_ctx_t *ctx,
                              uint32_t type,
                              uint64_t place,
                              uint64_t sym_value,
                              int64_t addend,
                              uint64_t *out_value) {
    int64_t result;

    switch (type) {
    case R_X86_64_64:
        *out_value = sym_value + addend;
        return 0;

    case R_X86_64_PC32:
    case R_X86_64_PLT32:
        result = sym_value + addend - place;
        if (result < -0x80000000LL || result > 0x7FFFFFFFLL) {
            return -1;
        }
        *out_value = (uint64_t)(int32_t)result;
        return 0;

    case R_X86_64_32:
        result = sym_value + addend;
        if (result < 0 || result > 0xFFFFFFFFLL) {
            return -1;
        }
        *out_value = (uint64_t)result;
        return 0;

    case R_X86_64_32S:
        result = sym_value + addend;
        if (result < -0x80000000LL || result > 0x7FFFFFFFLL) {
            return -1;
        }
        *out_value = (uint64_t)(int32_t)result;
        return 0;

    default:
        return -1;
    }
}

static int x86_64_reloc_size(uint32_t type) {
    switch (type) {
    case R_X86_64_64:
        return 8;
    case R_X86_64_PC32:
    case R_X86_64_PLT32:
    case R_X86_64_32:
    case R_X86_64_32S:
        return 4;
    default:
        return -1;
    }
}

static int x86_64_is_pc_relative(uint32_t type) {
    switch (type) {
    case R_X86_64_PC32:
    case R_X86_64_PLT32:
    case R_X86_64_GOTPCREL:
        return 1;
    default:
        return 0;
    }
}

int register_x86_64_backend(void) {
    static const struct elf_reloc_backend backend = {
        .machine = EM_X86_64,
        .apply_reloc = x86_64_apply_reloc,
        .reloc_size = x86_64_reloc_size,
        .is_pc_relative = x86_64_is_pc_relative,
    };

    return elf_register_reloc_backend(&backend) == ELF_OK ? 0 : -1;
}
.Ed
.Ss Using Backends for Relocation Processing
.Bd -literal
#include <elfobj.h>
#include <stdio.h>

/*
 * Example: Manually apply a relocation using the backend API.
 * This is for demonstration; normally the library handles this.
 */
void demonstrate_relocation(void) {
    elfobj_reloc_ctx_t ctx = {
        .machine = EM_386,
        .use_rela = 1,
    };

    /* Simulate applying R_386_PC32 relocation */
    uint64_t place = 0x1000;      /* Address of relocation site */
    uint64_t sym_value = 0x2000;  /* Symbol address */
    int64_t addend = -4;          /* Addend */
    uint64_t result;

    /* The backend would compute: sym_value + addend - place */
    /* = 0x2000 + (-4) - 0x1000 = 0xFFC */
    result = sym_value + addend - place;

    printf("R_386_PC32: S=0x%llx A=%lld P=0x%llx -> 0x%llx\\n",
           (unsigned long long)sym_value,
           (long long)addend,
           (unsigned long long)place,
           (unsigned long long)result);
}
.Ed
.Ss Backend with Overflow Detection
.Bd -literal
#include <elfobj.h>
#include <stdint.h>

/*
 * Helper function for signed overflow detection.
 * Returns 1 if value fits in n-bit signed integer.
 */
static int fits_signed(int64_t value, int bits) {
    int64_t min = -(1LL << (bits - 1));
    int64_t max = (1LL << (bits - 1)) - 1;
    return value >= min && value <= max;
}

/*
 * Helper function for unsigned overflow detection.
 * Returns 1 if value fits in n-bit unsigned integer.
 */
static int fits_unsigned(uint64_t value, int bits) {
    uint64_t max = (bits >= 64) ? UINT64_MAX : ((1ULL << bits) - 1);
    return value <= max;
}

static int safe_apply_32bit(uint64_t sym, int64_t addend,
                            uint64_t place, int is_pc_rel,
                            uint64_t *out) {
    int64_t result;

    if (is_pc_rel) {
        result = (int64_t)sym + addend - (int64_t)place;
    } else {
        result = (int64_t)sym + addend;
    }

    if (!fits_signed(result, 32)) {
        return -1;  /* Overflow */
    }

    *out = (uint64_t)(int32_t)result;
    return 0;
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr elf_reloc 3 ,
.Xr elfobj 3 ,
.Xr elf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
Relocation types and semantics follow the architecture-specific ELF
supplements.
See
.Xr elf_reloc 3
for references.
.Sh HISTORY
The backend plugin interface was added to
.Nm libelfobj
to support multiple target architectures without requiring modifications
to the core library for each new architecture.
.Sh BUGS
.Bl -bullet
.It
There is no way to enumerate registered backends.
.It
There is no way to unregister a backend.
.It
The maximum number of backends (16) is fixed at compile time.
.It
Backend callbacks cannot return detailed error information.
.El
